# SuperMox apt origin pins, installed at /etc/apt/preferences.d/supermox-origins
# by the supermox-ve package. This file is the single source of truth: the build
# VM (scripts/vm-setup-proxmox-repos.sh) and the ISO chroot (scripts/build-iso.sh)
# copy it instead of carrying their own text.
#
# Every pin here is structural, not a version hold: nothing keeps a Proxmox
# package behind the version upstream ships today. They only decide which origin
# a package may come from - our sysvinit rebuilds in front of Proxmox's systemd
# based builds, and systemd itself out altogether.

Explanation: SuperMox ships its own rebuilt PVE stack; local .debs must win.
Package: *
Pin: origin ""
Pin-Priority: 999

Explanation: Proxmox's trixie pve and devel repositories fill in the rest.
Package: *
Pin: origin download.proxmox.com
Pin-Priority: 100

Explanation: qemu-server needs Proxmox's patched swtpm (0.10.2+pve1), not Devuan's.
Package: swtpm swtpm-libs swtpm-tools
Pin: origin download.proxmox.com
Pin-Priority: 600

Explanation: these are the packages SuperMox rebuilds with its sysvinit patches,
 so an upstream Proxmox build of the same name must never replace one of ours:
 the Proxmox origin is refused outright (-1) for exactly these names, and only
 the local SuperMox repository (origin "", 999 above) may provide them.
# Component -> package(s) it builds; the names are not always identical.
# proxmox-perl-rs builds pve-rs from its pve-rs subdir (config/build-subdirs.txt);
# proxmox-ve is upstream's meta package, which SuperMox replaces with supermox-ve
# (that package Provides: proxmox-ve); every other component builds one package
# of its own name. Components are the directories under patches/ plus the ones
# config/upstream-overrides.txt pins to an upstream commit without a patch yet.
#   proxmox-perl-rs -> pve-rs
#   pve-cluster -> pve-cluster
#   pve-common -> pve-common
#   pve-container -> pve-container
#   pve-firewall -> pve-firewall
#   pve-ha-manager -> pve-ha-manager
#   pve-manager -> pve-manager
#   pve-storage -> pve-storage
#   qemu-server -> qemu-server
#   pve-access-control -> pve-access-control
#   pve-guest-common -> pve-guest-common
#   pve-http-server -> pve-http-server
#   proxmox-ve -> proxmox-ve
#   librados2-perl -> librados2-perl
Package: pve-rs pve-cluster pve-common pve-container pve-firewall pve-ha-manager pve-manager pve-storage qemu-server pve-access-control pve-guest-common pve-http-server proxmox-ve librados2-perl
Pin: origin download.proxmox.com
Pin-Priority: -1

Explanation: ZERO systemd. sysvinit-core and the standalone sysusers/tmpfiles
 binaries installed at bootstrap stay; nothing may pull systemd in later.
Package: systemd systemd-sysv libsystemd0 libpam-systemd libsystemd-twitch-1 libsystemd-twitch2 systemd-notify systemd-loginctl
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1
